Phase 3 agent half: the MCP shim. Standalone Python MCP stdio server harnesses/base/mcp_android.py (NOT merged into mcp_xpressclaw.py because that server wraps every result as TEXT — screenshot needs IMAGE content, so a separate server controls its own tools/call framing). Tools prefixed android_* (screenshot/tap_text/tap/swipe/type/key/dump); screenshot returns {type:image,mimeType:image/png,data:b64}; tap_text steered as preferred (accessibility tree, not pixel guesses). Proxies via httpx to XPRESSCLAW_URL (default host.docker.internal:8935) /v1/android/* — no adb in container.

Wired: default_mcp_servers() adds the 'android' stdio server (python3 -u /app/mcp_android.py) ONLY under #[cfg(feature=android)]; baked into base harness image via Dockerfile COPY. So every agent in an android-featured runtime gets the tools (refinement TODO: gate to agents bound to an android device/connector, + an android-pilot role/template that says 'screenshot before acting, prefer tap_text').

TO TEST THE AGENT PATH END-TO-END you need BOTH: (1) harness image rebuilt with mcp_android.py (done in this session), AND (2) the SERVER rebuilt --features android so default_mcp_servers injects the android MCP server into the container's MCP_SERVERS env. The installer built earlier this session (before this commit) does NOT inject it — rebuild the installer/server --features android. Then run an agent + tell it to do something on the device; it shares the same device as the human live view. Remaining: Phase 5 emulator lifecycle (android up/down provisioning via DEFAULT_SYSTEM_IMAGE). Not pushed.
